{
  "body_human_readable": "### \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy\" Movie Finances Revealed\n\nThe 2005 film adaptation of Douglas Adams' beloved science fiction comedy, \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy,\" was produced with a budget estimated to be between $45 and $50 million. The movie went on to achieve a worldwide box office gross of approximately $104.5 million.\n\nThe film, directed by Garth Jennings, was a much-anticipated project for fans of the original radio series and novels. The worldwide box office performance of the movie was more than double its production budget.\n\nIn its opening weekend in the United States, the movie topped the box office, earning an estimated $21.1 to $21.7 million. The domestic gross in the U.S. and Canada ultimately reached over $51 million. The international box office contributed over $53 million to the film's total earnings.",
